  "body": "An unrepaired compact-control parity word can restore its temporary fields while changing the target when used as its own return. With `G=2,K=6,x=1,y=33,t=3,b=2`, the target goes **33 \u2192 40 \u2192 41**, whereas the completed repaired operation cancels correctly. This is a **research note / scoped negative result**, not a defect in the retained repaired construction or a new kappa claim.\n\nThe package proves the exact one-digit formula, repeated-word failure support and orbit order, supplies a constructive isolated-pair correction, and retains the complete inherited recursive cost recurrence. It distinguishes raw reversal from ideal involution and does not assume a repair or child can commute across an interface.\n\nReproduce with standard-library Python 3.9+:\n\n```sh\npython3 -B research/compact-boundary-cancellation-seed51/verify.py\npython3 -B research/compact-boundary-cancellation-seed51/test_package.py\n```\n\nExpected: `PASS_COMPACT_BOUNDARY_CANCELLATION states=40800 production=1176 controls=8 no_new_kappa`, then `PASS_COMPACT_BOUNDARY_PACKAGE relocated_isolated_optimized=PASS faults=4`.\n\nValidation covers 40,800 complete small-domain states, 1,176 retained physical-interpreter comparisons, eight mathematical rejection controls, four injected package faults, and isolated optimized replay. The 22 affected existing tests passed at the analysis base. An independent Codex agent rederived the parity law and replayed the verifier/package with no blockers. Finite replay supports the written argument; it is not a formal proof of the multiplication theorem. Full repository suites, selected cold replay and hosted CI are separate and are not claimed.\n\nAnalysis base: `abdc6a7002abdbcd9e21bfc5e1a795784deacfdf`. Submission base: `ba82555c64e1879e4b7decce28186f208fcb8262`. Assignment seed **51**, OS CSPRNG, recursive interfaces. The original #942 selected record is pinned at its byte-identical historical checkpoint, so the verifier does not freeze the mutable selection pointer. All other pinned sources are unchanged between the two bases. The current #1042 conditional kappa **0.001672188119205421** and `upstream/` are unchanged.\n\nCredit Douglas Colkitt's compact-control construction/simulator and OpenAI's upstream framework. John-Michael Smith's #763 studies later-source interior carries; Precious Oyetunji's #773 and Aryan Sudhir's #735 study the distinct wide-slot gadget. This result adds the repeated **earlier-source** boundary law/support/order. #1012's T37 restoration mass and #1057's additive echo memory use different interfaces and are not imported. The refreshed 760-PR queue through #1105 contained no competing contribution on this precise object; the authenticated pinned-issue query returned no pinned coordination issue, so the claim is local.\n\nPrepared for **@martinxxx9** with substantial **OpenAI Codex assistance** in reasoning, implementation, verification and writing. Apache-2.0; retained predecessor attribution and all-size/compiler, hosting, fixed-tape, precision and analytic obligations remain explicit. Only `research/compact-boundary-cancellation-seed51/` is added.\n",
